          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you have <strong class="text-white">hard floors, a pet, a navigable floor plan and the budget for a self-emptying dock</strong>, a robot vacuum is among the best appliance purchases available. It removes a daily chore permanently and reaches places your upright never has.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your home is <strong class="text-white">thickly carpeted, permanently cluttered, or spread over several storeys on a tight budget</strong>, spend the money on a better conventional vacuum instead. And whichever you decide, keep the upright — the robot maintains floors; it does not deep clean them.
          </p>
